        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96347576?u=798adeac17b0340c3666d020c6f3391d71339849&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Added a sub-feature to <code class=\"notranslate\">html.elements.input.type_date</code> to indicate when browsers prevent picking dates outside the min/max range in the date picker UI.</p>\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">As cited in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3026356562\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/26656\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/26656/hovercard?comment_id=2867357979&amp;comment_type=issue_comment\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/26656#issuecomment-2867357979\">#26656 (comment)</a> .<br>\nPlease <a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/caugner/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/caugner\">@caugner</a>, confirm the versions.</p>\n\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n \n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #26656.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3026356562\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/26656\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/26656/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/26656\">#26656</a></p>\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27450",
            "title": "add disables_invalid_values_in_picker_ui sub-feature to input type=date",
            "date_modified": "2025-07-30T14:55:03.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-07-30T14:54:15.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "adi-ray",
                "url": "https://github.com/adi-ray"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36379249?u=4840c2d79361800483d4c22b03d928ae33115103&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">As discussed in <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1316857#c18\" rel=\"nofollow\">Mozilla Bug 1316857 comment 18</a>, the concept of \"same script\" is vague and likely inaccurate.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Additionally, to determine script-closeability, browsers switched from 'has an opener' to 'was opened by script' and that might be useful to note.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1316857#c18\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1316857#c18</a></p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"834043421\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/9492\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/9492/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/9492\">#9492</a></p>\n<hr>\n<p dir=\"auto\">My perception is these notes are usually quite short. Script-closeability also depends on the session history, so something like \"Before Chrome 95, scripts could only close windows that had an opener\" would be incorrect. I tried to omit this detail, but am unsure whether that made my phrasing too awkward. We could remove the notes entirely. An alternative phrasing might be \"Before Chrome 95, whether a window could be closed by script depended on having an opener, not on whether it was created by web content.\"</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27396",
            "title": "Revise notes for historic window.close() behavior",
            "date_modified": "2025-07-24T14:11:24.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-07-24T14:09:26.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "vinhill",
                "url": "https://github.com/vinhill"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5179191?u=8dd92441fba3cb438759ee98862670ba56f2c67d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">This PR updates and corrects version values for Chromium (Chrome, Opera, Samsung Internet, WebView Android) for the <code class=\"notranslate\">-webkit-slider-thumb</code> CSS selector. The data comes from manual testing, running test code through BrowserStack, SauceLabs, custom VMs and/or locally.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Test Code:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-css notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"::-webkit-slider-thumb {\n\tpadding: 1em;\n}\"><pre class=\"notranslate\">::<span class=\"pl-c1\">-webkit-slider-thumb</span> {\n\t<span class=\"pl-c1\">padding</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">:</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">1<span class=\"pl-smi\">em</span></span>;\n}</pre></div>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27391",
            "title": "Update Chromium data for -webkit-slider-thumb CSS selector",
            "date_modified": "2025-07-23T17:53:12.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-07-23T17:52:37.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "queengooborg",
                "url": "https://github.com/queengooborg"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5179191?u=8dd92441fba3cb438759ee98862670ba56f2c67d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">This PR updates and corrects version values for Chromium (Chrome, Opera, Samsung Internet, WebView Android) for the <code class=\"notranslate\">-webkit-slider-runnable-track</code> CSS selector. The data comes from manual testing, running test code through BrowserStack, SauceLabs, custom VMs and/or locally.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Test Code:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-css notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"::-webkit-slider-runnable-track {\n  background: linear-gradient(to right, black, white);\n}\"><pre class=\"notranslate\">::<span class=\"pl-c1\">-webkit-slider-runnable-track</span> {\n  <span class=\"pl-c1\">background</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">:</span> <span class=\"pl-en\">linear-gradient</span>(to right<span class=\"pl-kos\">,</span> black<span class=\"pl-kos\">,</span> white);\n}</pre></div>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27390",
            "title": "Update Chromium data for -webkit-slider-runnable-track CSS selector",
            "date_modified": "2025-07-23T17:50:16.000Z",
